[102.902811, "o", "\u001b[19dNow I have a clear picture of the codebase. Here is my implementation\r\n approach:\u001b[22;1H---\u001b[H\u001b[68C\u001b[1K\u001b[H### Files to create\u001b[2;69H\u001b[1K\r\n**1. `packages/api/src/components/pay/payment.types.ts`**\u001b[12X\r\nShared domain types for PaymentService (not duplicating types already\u001b[5;69H\u001b[1K\r in CardForm.tsx):\r\n- `PaymentStatus` (`pending | processing | succeeded | failed`)\u001b[6X\r\n- `PaymentRequest` — opaque token + amount + currency (never raw PAN)\r\n- `PaymentResult` — transactionId, status, amount, currency\u001b[10X\r\n- `PaymentServiceError` — typed error with `code` + `retryable` flag\u001b[1X\r\n- `PaymentServiceConfig` — endpoint, maxRetries, timeoutMs\u001b[11X\u001b[11;69H\u001b[1K\r\n**2. `packages/api/src/components/pay/PaymentService.ts`**\u001b[11X\r\nA class that posts tokenized payment requests to the backend:\u001b[8X\r\n- `submit(request: PaymentRequest): Promise<PaymentResult>` — POSTs t\u001b[15;69H\u001b[1K\ro configured endpoint\r\n- Internal `fetchWithRetry` — retries up to `maxRetries` times on net\r\nwork errors / 5xx, never on 4xx (card declined, etc.)\u001b[16X\r\n- `AbortController`-based timeout per attempt\u001b[24X\r\n- **PCI-DSS**: raw card fields never enter this class — it only ever \r\nsees the opaque `token` from the processor SDK\u001b[23X\r\n- TypeScript strict mode throughout\u001b[34X\u001b[22;69H\u001b[1K\r\n**3. `packages/api/tests/unit/PaymentService.test.ts`**\u001b[14X\u001b[H"]
